          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768421011651_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_SCHEDULE_CONTEXT_EXTRACTOR.$output.handoffReady}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7153.25,
            "y": 6592
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Schedule Context Extractor"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770325296155"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_SCHEDULE_CONTEXT_EXTRACTOR",
          "id": "1768421342943",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768421342944_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Input Context\n\n- User Input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- Chat History: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\n- Current Date: {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n- Current Date and Time: {{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}} \n\n------\n\n## Objective\n\nBased on the **user input** and **chat history**, classify the scheduling request into **exactly one** supported `scheduleType` and populate the required slots accordingly.\n\n------\n\n\n## Steps to Execute\n\n### 1. Identify scheduleType and Extract Required Slots\n\nYou must classify the request into **one and only one** of the following schedule types. And try to extract required slots from user input. For slots that are not required for the current scheduleType or user doesn't clearly mention, leave them as empty.\n\n------\n\n#### A. oneTimePprScheduleRequest\n\n**Required slots:**\n\n- startTime \n- submitReport\n- pprTemplate \n\n\n------\n\n#### B. recurringPprScheduleRequest\n\n**Required slots:**\n\n- startTime\n- endTime \n- frequency \n- submitReport\n- pprTemplate \n\n\n------\n\n### 2. (IMPORTANT) Override the Current Extracted Slots:\n\n**You must first inspect the currently extracted slots:**\n\n- scheduleType: {{$context.$variables.scheduleType}}\n- submitReport: {{$context.$variables.submitReport}}\n- startTime: {{$context.$variables.startTime}}\n- endTime: {{$context.$variables.endTime}}\n- frequency: {{$context.$variables.frequency}}\n- pprTemplate: {{$context.$variables.pprTemplate}}\n\n\nFor each scheduling slot (scheduleType, startTime, endTime, frequency, submitReport, pprTemplate):\n\n1. Based on user input and chat history, determine whether the user has explicitly specified a value for the slot in the natural language input.\n\n   - Explicit means the user clearly mentions the value or gives an unambiguous instruction.\n   - Do NOT infer or fabricate values that the user did not mention.\n\n2. If the user explicitly specifies a value for the slot AND it differs from the current extracted value:\n\n   - Override the existing slot value with the value inferred from the user input.\n\n3. If the user does NOT explicitly specify the slot:\n\n   - Keep the existing slot value if it is already populated.\n   - Otherwise, apply the default rules defined below.\n\n\n\n4. Never keep conflicting values between the user input and the slot variables.\n   The final slot values must always reflect the user’s intent as expressed in the user input.\n\n5. Exactly one scheduleType must be selected.\n\n   - If the user input implies a different scheduleType than the current one, override scheduleType.\n   - When scheduleType changes, recompute all required and forbidden slots accordingly.\n\n6. For pprTemplate, intelligently Identify substrings that could reasonably refer to a PPR Template name. A substring may be considered a PPR Template candidate if it:\n\n   - Looks like a system-defined or user-defined template name\n\n   - Contains patterns such as uppercase letters, underscores, numbers, or dots\n     (e.g., CPPRT_020015, LLI_Electronic, PPR_WEEKLY_RUN)\n\n   - Is referenced in a scheduling or payment context\n\n   - Is explicitly mentioned after words like \"template\", \"use\", \"run\", \"based on\", \"schedule a run with\"\n\nPartial PPR template name rule:\t\nIf the user refers to a template by partial-name language such as \"has <value> in its name\", \"contains <value>\", \"matching <value>\", \"similar to <value>\", or \"starts with <value>\", populate pprTemplate with <value>.\t\nDo not treat pprTemplate as missing in this case. The value is a search key that can be used to find matching PPR templates.\t\nExample:\t\nUser: There is a PPR template that has BCH in its name. Use that to run PPR.\t\npprTemplate: \"BCH\"\n\n7. For startTime:\n     - Always use UTC. If the user provides a timezone other than UTC, convert it to UTC.\n     - If the user specifies a clear start DATE but omits the time (e.g., \"starting tomorrow\", \"starting next Monday\"), infer the start time using the current date and time as reference (in UTC).\n     - Always output the start time in ISO-8601 format like \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ\".\n     - If the user provides a time explicitly, use it (converted to UTC) and format as ISO-8601.\n\n8. For endTime\n   - Always use UTC; convert if another timezone is given.\n   - If endTime is relative (e.g., \"next Friday\", \"in 3 months\", \"after 90 days\", \"end after 1 year\"), resolve it using startTime if available; otherwise use current UTC time.\n   - Output ISO-8601: \"YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ\".\n   - If time is provided, use it (converted to UTC).\n9. If the frequency input is not recognized or cannot be converted into a valid RRULE icalString, do not populate frequency (set to \"\").\n\n#### Hard constraints:\n\n- Do NOT fabricate endTime or frequency.\n  These values must be explicitly provided by the user for recurring schedules.\n\n- If scheduleType = oneTimePprScheduleRequest:\n  - endTime and frequency must be empty.\n\n- If scheduleType = recurringPprScheduleRequest:\n  - endTime and frequency must be present.\n\n\n---\n\n### 3. Output Slot Data with JSON Structure \n\nBased on the overriden result from step 2, try to extract all required slots for according scheduleType. Leave the missing and unnecessary configurations empty. Return the following structure exactly as defined below:\n\n{\n\"scheduleType\": \"\",\n\"startTime\": \"\",\n\"endTime\": \"\",\n\"frequency\": \"\",\n\"submitReport\": \"\",\n\"pprTemplate\": \"\",\n\"contextStatus\": \"pending\",\n\"handoffReady\": false,\n\"responseToUser\": \"\"\n}\n\n------\n\n## Slot Filling Rules\n\n- Never fabricate, guess, or infer slot values.\n- Only populate slots when the value is **explicitly provided** by the user.\n- Use both the **current user input** and **extracted slots** to determine whether a slot has already been filled.\n- Leave any missing slot as an empty string (`\"\"`).\n\n------\n\n## Completion Logic\n\n### When all required slots for the selected `scheduleType` are filled:\n\n- Set:\n  - `contextStatus` = `\"ready\"`\n  - `handoffReady` = `true`\n  - `responseToUser` = `\"\"`\n\n------\n\n### When one or more required slots are missing:\n\n- Set:\n  - `contextStatus` = `\"pending\"`\n  - `handoffReady` = `false`\n- Populate `responseToUser` with:\n  - A **single, concise clarification question**, no more than 3 sentences.\n  - Ask **only** for the missing required slot(s).\n  - Avoid explanations, system details, examples, or repetition.\n\n\n------\n\n## Response Guidelines\n\n- Do not include internal reasoning or classification explanations in the response.\n- Do not reference schemas, validation logic, or system rules.\n- Keep user-facing questions brief, polite, and actionable."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"handoffReady\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"responseToUser\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"scheduleType\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"oneTimePprScheduleRequest\",\n        \"recurringPprScheduleRequest\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"startTime\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"endTime\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"frequency\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"submitReport\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"pprTemplate\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"contextStatus\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n        \"pending\",\n        \"ready\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
