          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768434347684_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "1) scheduleType: {{$context.$variables.scheduleType}}\n2) startTime: {{$context.$variables.startTime}}\n3) endTime: {{$context.$variables.endTime}}\n4) frequency: {{$context.$variables.frequency}}\n5) submitReport: {{$context.$variables.submitReport}} \n\nYour responsibility is to format the output to be shown to the user:\n- Inform the user that no payment process request template was identified based on user message. Ask user to try another different PPR template\n- When rendering the output, all column name should be changed to human-friendly name and do not use abbreviation, e.g. scheduleType -> Schedule Type, pprTemplate -> Payment Process Request Template, submitReport -> Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\n- Start Time and End Time (if provided) must be non-empty strings in ISO 8601 UTC format (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ).\n- When presenting Frequency, use these wording rules:\n    - If the schedule repeats every week, say: \"Weekly, on <day or days>\"\n    - If the schedule repeats every N weeks and N is greater than 1, say: \"Every N weeks on <day or days>\"\n    - If the schedule repeats every day, say: \"Daily\"\n    - If the schedule repeats every N days and N is greater than 1, say: \"Every N days\"\n    - If the schedule repeats every month, say: \"Monthly\" or \"Monthly, on day <date>\" when a day of month is present\n    - If the schedule repeats every N months and N is greater than 1, say: \"Every N months\" or \"Every N months on day <date>\"\n    - Never combine both styles in one phrase. Do not say \"Weekly, every 2 weeks on Monday\" or \"Weekly, every 4 weeks on Thursday\"\n    - Do not use shorthand labels such as \"Biweekly\". Prefer explicit wording like \"Every 2 weeks on Monday\"\n\nStrictly follow the JSON output format like below:\n\nExample 1 - for one-time schedule:\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"<Your content to let user know no Payment Process Request template was identified and ask user to try another different PPR template. And tell them the following table contents are the schedule configurations you already stored>\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"table\",\n    \"columnOrder\": [\"Schedule Type\", \"Payment Process Request Template\", \"Start Time\", \"Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\"],\n    \"heading\": \"Payment Process Request Schedule Configurations\",\n    \"content\": [\n      {\n        \"Schedule Type\": \"Recurring\",\n        \"Payment Process Request Template\": \"\",\n        \"Start Time\": \"2025-02-12T00:00:00Z\",\n        \"Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\": \"Y\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"Alternatively, if you prefer to create a new request from scratch without using a template, you can use the link below: {deeplink:{objType:AP_SUBMITPPR,action:CREATE, text:Submit Payment Process Request}}\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 3\n  }\n]\n\nExample 2 - for recurring schedule:\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"<Your content to let user know no Payment Process Request template was identified and ask user to try another different PPR template. And tell them the following table contents are the schedule configurations you already stored>\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"table\",\n    \"columnOrder\": [\"Schedule Type\", \"Payment Process Request Template\", \"Start Time\", \"End Time\", \"Frequency\", \"Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\"],\n    \"heading\": \"Payment Process Request Schedule Configurations\",\n    \"content\": [\n      {\n        \"Schedule Type\": \"Recurring\",\n        \"Payment Process Request Template\": \"\",\n        \"Start Time\": \"2025-02-12T00:00:00Z\",\n        \"End Time\": \"2026-02-11T00:00:00Z\",\n        \"Frequency\": \"Weekly, on Tuesday\",\n        \"Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\": \"Y\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"Alternatively, if you prefer to create a new request from scratch without using a template, you can use the link below: {deeplink:{objType:AP_SUBMITPPR,action:CREATE, text:Submit Payment Process Request}}\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 3\n  }\n]\n\nStrictly follow this JSON structure for your output. Do not include any Markdown, HTML, or any other format or text outside the JSON array."
