          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_CHECK_USER_APPROVAL",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1768421011650",
          "id": "1770326514285",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770326514286_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "User Input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nChat History: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.chatHistory}}\nhandoffReady: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_SCHEDULE_CONTEXT_EXTRACTOR.$output.handoffReady}}\ntemplateId: {{$context.$variables.templateId}} \n\n### Identified \"userApproval\" Slot\n\nBased on the content from user input and chat history, and \"handoffReady\" slot, identify if user approved or disapproved the payment process request run schedule and output the corresponding \"userApproval\" slot.\n\nJudging Rules (IMPORTANT):\n1. If handoffReady is false:\n   - userApproval -> pending\n2. If handoffReady is true:\n   - Approve:\n     - The user explicitly expresses approval intent and includes any of these keywords (case-insensitive): \"approve\", \"approved\", \"confirm\", \"confirmed\", with \"confirm\" and \"approve\" treated as a strong signal\n     - No negation is present (e.g., \"not approve\", \"do not approve\", \"disapprove\", \"reject\", \"cancel\", \"decline\", \"deny\", \"not confirm\")\n     - templateId is not null or empty\n     - Then userApproval -> approved\n   - Disapprove:\n     - The user explicitly expresses rejection/negative intent using any of these keywords (case-insensitive): \"cancel\", \"disapprove\", \"reject\", \"decline\", \"deny\", with \"cancel\" treated as a strong signal\n     - Or negation combined with approve/confirm (e.g., \"do not approve\", \"don't approve\", \"not confirm\")\n     - Then userApproval -> disapproved\n   - Otherwise:\n     - The user is changing some schedule configurations, like \"do not submit the report\", \"change the start time to next Monday\", \"changed the schedule type as recurring\". No matter what the user approved or disapproved, the user approval -> pending\n     - userApproval -> pending\n     \n3. Additional guardrails and precedence:\n   - Only explicit approval keywords count. Expressions like \"ok\", \"proceed\", \"go ahead\", \"sounds good\", \"agree\", emojis, or likes do NOT count as approval; return pending.\n   - If both approval and disapproval signals appear, disapproval takes precedence.\n   - Use the latest user message for intent. System/assistant prompts do not count as user intent."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"userApproval\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 7153.25,
            "y": 6370
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.25
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Output Formatter for Asking Human Approval"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771537472911"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_OUTPUT_FORMATTER_FOR_ASKING_HUMAN_APPROVAL",
          "id": "1770328518160",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770328518164_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "1) scheduleType: {{$context.$variables.scheduleType}}\n2) pprTemplate: {{$context.$variables.pprTemplate}}\n3) startTime: {{$context.$variables.startTime}}\n4) endTime: {{$context.$variables.endTime}}\n5) frequency: {{$context.$variables.frequency}}\n6) submitReport: {{$context.$variables.submitReport}} \n\nYour responsibility is to format the output to be shown to the user:\n- User polite and professional tone to inform the user that the Payment Process Request run is scheduled as requested, and ask user to approve the run by inputting Approve\n- You still need to render a table that contains \"schedule configurations\" excluding pprTemplate:\n     - If the scheduleType is \"oneTimePprScheduleRequest\", render \"scheduleType\", \"pprTemplate\", \"startTime\",  \"submitReport\" as a table.\n     - If the scheduleType is \"recurringPprScheduleRequest\", render \"scheduleType\", \"pprTemplate\", \"startTime\", \"endTime\", \"frequency\",  \"submitReport\" as a table.\n- When rendering the output, all column name should be changed to human-friendly name and do not use abbreviation, e.g. scheduleType -> Schedule Type, pprTemplate -> Payment Process Request Template, submitReport -> Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\n- Start Time and End Time (if provided) must be non-empty strings in ISO 8601 UTC format (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ).\n- For RRULE syntax (FREQ=, BYDAY=, BYHOUR=...) in Frequency, you should present it in a human-readable text in final response. When presenting Frequency, use the below wording rules:\n  - If the schedule repeats every week, say: \"Weekly, on <day or days>\"\n  - If the schedule repeats every N weeks and N is greater than 1, say: \"Every N weeks on <day or days>\"\n  - If the schedule repeats every day, say: \"Daily\"\n  - If the schedule repeats every N days and N is greater than 1, say: \"Every N days\"\n  - If the schedule repeats every month, say: \"Monthly\" or \"Monthly, on day <date>\" when a day of month is present\n  - If the schedule repeats every N months and N is greater than 1, say: \"Every N months\" or \"Every N months on day <date>\"\n  - Never combine both styles in one phrase. Do not say \"Weekly, every 2 weeks on Monday\" or \"Weekly, every 4 weeks on Thursday\"\n  - Do not use shorthand labels such as \"Biweekly\". Prefer explicit wording like \"Every 2 weeks on Monday\"\n- Strictly follow the JSON output format like below. Do not miss any necessary columns:\n\nExample 1 - for one-time schedule:\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"<Your content to let user know the Payment Process Request run is scheduled as requested, and ask user to approve the run by inputting Approve>\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"table\",\n    \"columnOrder\": [\"Schedule Type\", \"Payment Process Request Template\", \"Start Time\", \"Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\"],\n    \"heading\": \"Payment Process Request Schedule Configurations\",\n    \"content\": [\n      {\n        \"Schedule Type\": \"Recurring\",\n        \"Payment Process Request Template\": \"CPPRT_020015\",\n        \"Start Time\": \"2025-02-12T00:00:00Z\",\n        \"Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\": \"Y\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"actions\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"Approve the Payment Process Request run\",\n      \"Cancel the Payment Process Request run\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 3\n  }\n]\n\nExample 2 - for recurring schedule:\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"<Your content to let user know the Payment Process Request run schedule is scheduled as requested, and ask user to approve the run by input Approve.>\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"table\",\n    \"columnOrder\": [\"Schedule Type\", \"Payment Process Request Template\", \"Start Time\", \"End Time\", \"Frequency\", \"Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\"],\n    \"heading\": \"Payment Process Request Schedule Configurations\",\n    \"content\": [\n      {\n        \"Schedule Type\": \"Recurring\",\n        \"Payment Process Request Template\": \"CPPRT_020015\",\n        \"Start Time\": \"2025-02-12T00:00:00Z\",\n        \"End Time\": \"2026-02-11T00:00:00Z\",\n        \"Frequency\": \"Weekly, on Tuesday\",\n        \"Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\": \"Y\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"actions\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"Approve the Payment Process Request run\",\n      \"Cancel the Payment Process Request run\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 3\n  }\n]"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
