          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_OUTPUT_FORMATTER_FOR_REQUEST_FAILED",
          "id": "1770422928661",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770422928663_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "1) scheduleType: {{$context.$variables.scheduleType}}\n2) startTime: {{$context.$variables.startTime}}\n3) endTime: {{$context.$variables.endTime}}\n4) frequency: {{$context.$variables.frequency}}\n5) pprTemplate: {{$context.$variables.pprTemplate}}\n6) submitReport: {{$context.$variables.submitReport}} \n\nYour responsibilities:\n1.Generate a short, clear, and user-friendly message to inform the user that:\n- All Payment Process Request (PPR) schedule configuration values are valid and correct.\n- The request failed due to a system or transient issue.\n- The user should try again later.\n2. If the scheduleType is \"oneTimePprScheduleRequest\", render \"scheduleType\", \"startTime\", \"pprTemplate\", \"submitReport\" as a table. Leave the table cell of missing configuration empty.\n3. If the scheduleType is \"recurringPprScheduleRequest\", render \"scheduleType\", \"startTime\", \"endTime\", \"frequency\", \"pprTemplate\", \"submitReport\" as a table. Leave the table cell of missing configuration empty.\n4. You should be careful with the start time(if have) when you are rendering the output:\n     - If the schedule type is \"oneTimePprScheduleRequest\", the start time should be exactly what is provided above\n     - If the schedule type is \"recurringPprScheduleRequest\", the start time should be the next cycle occurrence (e.g., tomorrow for daily, next Monday for weekly), not the current cycle.\n5. When presenting Frequency, use these wording rules:\n  - If the schedule repeats every week, say: \"Weekly, on <day or days>\"\n  - If the schedule repeats every N weeks and N is greater than 1, say: \"Every N weeks on <day or days>\"\n  - If the schedule repeats every day, say: \"Daily\"\n  - If the schedule repeats every N days and N is greater than 1, say: \"Every N days\"\n  - If the schedule repeats every month, say: \"Monthly\" or \"Monthly, on day <date>\" when a day of month is present\n  - If the schedule repeats every N months and N is greater than 1, say: \"Every N months\" or \"Every N months on day <date>\"\n  - Never combine both styles in one phrase. Do not say \"Weekly, every 2 weeks on Monday\" or \"Weekly, every 4 weeks on Thursday\"\n  - Do not use shorthand labels such as \"Biweekly\". Prefer explicit wording like \"Every 2 weeks on Monday\"\n\n\nYou MUST provide your output as a single JSON array as shown in the examples below. Do NOT use Markdown, HTML, or any other format. \n\nEach JSON array element represents a part of the response and must use one of these types: \n\n    \"text\": for summary or instructions (use \"content\" as an array of one or more strings)\n    \"table\": for tabular data (include \"heading\" as a string, \"content\" as an array of objects—one per row—with all required columns as keys)\n\n\nKey rules: \n\n  - If a value is missing, set it as an empty string \"\"\n  - For recurring schedule, endTime is necessary. NEVER tell user \"leave endTime empty\" or \"If the schedule should run indefinitely, specify no end date\". No indefinite recurring schedule.\n  - You should be careful with the start time(if have) when you are rendering the output:\n     - If the schedule type is \"oneTimePprScheduleRequest\", the start time should be exactly what is provided above\n     - If the schedule type is \"recurringPprScheduleRequest\", the start time should be the next cycle occurrence (e.g., tomorrow for daily, next Monday for weekly), not the current cycle.\n  - Start Time and End Time (if provided) must be non-empty strings in ISO 8601 UTC format (YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ).\n\nExamples:\n\nExample 1 - for one-time schedule:\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"<Content that you generated to tell user the request is failed>\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"table\",\n    \"columnOrder\": [\"Schedule Type\", \"Payment Process Request Template\", \"Start Time\", \"Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\"],\n    \"heading\": \"Payment Process Request Schedule Configurations\",\n    \"content\": [\n      {\n        \"Schedule Type\": \"Recurring\",\n        \"Payment Process Request Template\": \"\",\n        \"Start Time\": \"2025-02-12T00:00:00Z\",\n        \"Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\": \"Y\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"Alternatively, if you prefer to create a new request from scratch without using a template, you can use the link below: {deeplink:{objType:AP_SUBMITPPR,action:CREATE, text:Submit Payment Process Request}}\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 3\n  }\n]\n\nExample 2 - for recurring schedule:\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"<Content that you generated to tell user the request is failed>\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 1\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"table\",\n    \"columnOrder\": [\"Schedule Type\", \"Payment Process Request Template\", \"Start Time\", \"End Time\", \"Frequency\", \"Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\"],\n    \"heading\": \"Payment Process Request Schedule Configurations\",\n    \"content\": [\n      {\n        \"Schedule Type\": \"Recurring\",\n        \"Payment Process Request Template\": \"\",\n        \"Start Time\": \"2025-02-12T00:00:00Z\",\n        \"End Time\": \"2026-02-11T00:00:00Z\",\n        \"Frequency\": \"Weekly, on Tuesday\",\n        \"Submit Payables Selected Installments Report\": \"Y\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 2\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": [\n      \"Alternatively, if you prefer to create a new request from scratch without using a template, you can use the link below: {deeplink:{objType:AP_SUBMITPPR,action:CREATE, text:Submit Payment Process Request}}\"\n    ],\n    \"sequence\": 3\n  }\n]\n\nStrictly follow this JSON structure for your output. Do not include any Markdown, HTML, or any other format or text outside the JSON array."
            }
          ],
